# Verify against CI before finishing

GitHub `Test` runs `format:check` then `test:e2e --project=desktop-chrome`. Do not finish a change that will be committed or pushed until both pass locally — including copy/content edits. Flaky scroll/nav failures often show up only under CI load; skip this and CI keeps failing.

## Before you stop (commit / push / “hotovo”)

1. `pnpm exec prettier --write` on touched files (or `pnpm run format:check`).
2. Run full desktop Chrome E2E (not only “related” specs) when pushing to `main`:

```bash
pnpm exec playwright test --project=desktop-chrome
```

During iteration on hero / scroll / sticky nav, at least:

```bash
pnpm exec playwright test tests/e2e/carousel.spec.ts tests/e2e/navigation.desktop.spec.ts --project=desktop-chrome
```

## Scroll assertions

- Prefer two-arg `window.scrollTo(0, y)` — `html { scroll-behavior: smooth }` ignores `behavior: 'instant'|'auto'` in Chromium.
- Prefer `expect.poll` on `scrollY` / `aria-current` over fixed `waitForTimeout`.
- Hero scroll cue is `absolute` inside `#hero`; scroll past `hero.offsetHeight`, not a fixed pixel delta.
